2025-12-28
Update: serve-ssr starts and listens, but browser/curl requests to / hang indefinitely.
Hypothesis: SSR render promise never resolves because the app never becomes stable.
Finding: HomepageComponent creates a periodic RxJS timer (timer(0, 3000)) in its constructor; if the template subscribes (async pipe), this schedules endless macroTasks and SSR never completes.
Fix (done): In HomepageComponent, only create the periodic timer in the browser; on the server use a single-emission observable (of(0)).
Next: Re-run serve-ssr and verify that curl returns HTML quickly; then check browser render/hydration.

2026-01-03
Update: Navbar SSR rendered both mobile + desktop variants because `*appBreakpoints` always rendered content during SSR.
Fix (done): Make `BreakpointsDirective` evaluate breakpoint conditions during SSR using an assumed viewport width (InjectionToken `SSR_VIEWPORT_WIDTH`, default 1025px) instead of always rendering.
Next: Re-run serve-ssr and confirm server HTML only includes one breakpoint branch for navbar/logo/search.

2026-01-10
Update: Navbar logo + theme toggle showed "both states" on first render due to theme being resolved only after Angular bootstrap (localStorage/matchMedia in AppComponent).
Fix (done):
- Add an early theme bootstrap script in apps/commudle-admin/src/index.html to set documentElement[data-theme] before first paint.
- Make navbar theme variants CSS-driven (show/hide via :host-context([data-theme='dark'])) rather than *ngIf on isDarkMode.
- Harden DarkModeService.toggleDarkMode to guard localStorage/document in SSR and keep data-theme in sync in the browser.
Next: Run serve-ssr and verify navbar/logo/toggle no longer flicker or double-render on initial load.
